From: Luma Developers
Subject: [PATCH] One shadow per rule, as St paints

St paints one box-shadow per actor and parses only one layer: every value
after the fourth length is dropped with "Ignoring excess values in shadow
definition", and the last colour in the list wins. Multi-layer rules on the
lock and login poster (card, avatar, password field and its focus ring, away
well), the Quick Options radio hover and the dock icons therefore painted
the first layer's geometry in another layer's colour (the dock icons and the
poster card got a dark inset line) and filled the journal with warnings
whenever those nodes were restyled. Each rule now names the one layer it
was designed around: the outset depth shadow, the focus ring, or the inset
outline where a rule has only inset layers.

